<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Spending ===
Users can spend their VRChat Credits on the {{VRC link|https://vrchat.com/home/marketplace/welcome |website}}, or in the client, through either, the [[Special:MyLanguage/Shop|Shop]], or [[Special:MyLanguage/Avatars|avatar]], [[Special:MyLanguage/Groups|group]], or [[Special:MyLanguage/Worlds|world]] stores. Users can buy a listing or a subscription with their VRChat Credits, each listing and subscription has products attached to them, these are ''in layman's terms'' the benefits you receive from the listing or subscription.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The '''Spotlight''' section of the Marketplace tab offers suggestions of worlds and groups that are currently enrolled in the Creator Economy Program.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
For more creator-related information, see the Creator Economy documentation<ref>{{VRC link|https://creators.vrchat.com/economy/|Creator Economy Documentation}} from 24 May, 2024</ref>''.''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==== Stores ====
Stores are where users can buy content with VRChat Credits. There are 3 types of stores:
</div>
{| class="wikitable"
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Stores</span>
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Description</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Avatar Marketplace</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users can find all public avatar listings here. Located on the Avatar page, in the explore tab.</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">World</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Located on a world page, in the store tab. Users can buy content for the world they're in, or avatar listings.</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Group</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Located on a group page, in the store tab. Users can buy subscriptions that could grant them content without various worlds or a group role.</span>
|}
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==== Listings ====
Listings are what users can buy from stores. While listings can be anything the creator decides, users can expect to see common types of listing such as: Unlocking new areas of a world, customization options, and more.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
There are 3 types of listings creators can offer, each type has a different duration type.
</div>
{| class="wikitable"
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Listing</span>
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Duration</span>
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Description</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Instant</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">None</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users can purchase this type as many times as they want. Benefits are instantly awarded. This type is only purchasable if you are in the world.</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Temporary</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">5 minutes - 3 months</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users can purchase this type as many times as they want '''but''' can't repurchase until its duration expires. Benefits earned are only available until its duration expires.</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Permanent</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Unlimited</span>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users can only purchase this type once. Benefits are permanently available to the buyer.</span>
|}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===== Subscriptions =====
Subscriptions are the type of listing that users can buy from group stores. While listings can be anything the world creator decides, users can expect to see common types of listing such as: VIP access.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Users have 4 default duration options, they can choose from when buying a subscription.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* 1 month
* 3 months
* 6 months
* 12 months
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
There is also a custom duration option users can choose, which ranges from 1 month to 99 months. Subscriptions do not automatically renew.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
When a user buys a subscription, they will be automatically added to the group they bought the subscription from. Buyers will also a group role, which creators can offer group specific benefits.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==== Products ====
When users buy listings or subscriptions, they contain products (also referred to as "Benefits" in-game). Each listing or subscription can contain multiple products. Products have 3 types:
</div>
{| class="wikitable"
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Product type</span>
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Limitations</span>
!<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Description</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Avatar</span>

|<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Listing type must be: Permanent
* Can be sold in world stores, and the Avatar Marketplace
</div>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users receive said avatar in the Purchased tab of their My Avatars page on the Avatars page.</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Subscription Role</span>
|<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Listing type must be: Subscription
* Can only be sold in group stores
</div>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users receive a role in the group they bought the subscription in. It may grant additional group permissions such as access to viewing group posts, instances and/or priority queues.</span>
|-
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Udon</span>
|<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Listing type can be any
* Can only be sold in world and group stores
</div>
|<span lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">Users receive benefits in the world they bought the listing in. Common types of benefits include: VIP access, cosmetics, items, etc.</span>
|}

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Viewing transaction history ===
To view the history of your transactions, navigate to the '''Marketplace''' page on the [[Special:MyLanguage/Main Menu|Main Menu]], proceed to the '''Wallet''' section, and then choose the '''Transactions''' tab. Alternatively, you can view it on the {{VRC link|https://vrchat.com/home/marketplace/wallet |VRChat website}}.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The Transactions tab shows the history of the user's VRChat Credits on their account. Listing the name of the product, the amount of credits, the remaining balance after the purchase, the recipient, the date of purchase, and the type of transaction.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
To view your purchases or active and expired subscriptions, navigate to the '''Purchases & Subscriptions''' tab of the '''Marketplace''' page.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The Purchases tab lists any listing you bought, including its type, date of purchase and expiration, and details. While, the Subscriptions tab includes the same details as the Purchases tab, just instead for subscriptions. It is split up by an "Active" and "Expired" dropdown, and also includes an option to renew the subscription or cancel it.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
== Avatar Marketplace ==
''<small>See also: [[Special:MyLanguage/Avatar Marketplace|Avatar Marketplace]] for more detailed information.</small>''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The '''Avatar Marketplace''' is a feature announced by VRChat on {{Date|May 14, 2025}}<ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MWH1RA3bEz0 youtube.com]</ref><ref>[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/announcing-the-avatar-marketplace/43554 ask.vrchat.com]</ref>, as an expansion of the Creator Economy. This update introduces a native system for selling and buying avatars directly within VRChat using VRChat Credits.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
With the [[Special:MyLanguage/Avatar Marketplace|Avatar Marketplace]], users can purchase avatars that are automatically added to their VRChat account without the need to manually upload avatars through Unity. Purchased avatars are permanently accessible to the buyer outside of extraordinary circumstances. <!-- TODO: elaborate on extraordinary circumstances, like if the avatar contains TOS or potentially illegal content -->
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Avatars listed on the marketplace can be locally previewed before purchase, meaning the avatar is only visible to the user while using the try-on feature.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The Avatar Marketplace update adds three new upper tabs to the Avatars tab in the [[Special:MyLanguage/Main Menu|Main Menu]]. The '''Explore''' tab lets a user search for avatars for sale in the Marketplace, as well as varying categories of avatars for sale. The '''My Avatars''' tab utilizes the traditional avatar menu, with your uploaded avatars, favorited avatars, as well as a new section for "Purchased" avatars from the marketplace. Lastly, the '''My Current Avatar''' tab shows the avatar details of an avatar that you are currently wearing.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Users interested in [https://ask.vrchat.com/t/avatar-marketplace-faq-for-sellers/43555 selling avatars] on the Avatar Marketplace need to enroll in VRChat's Creator Economy Program for approval.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
== Enrolling in the Creator Economy Program ==
</div>

{{Thumb|{{YouTube|cNvmvPa4T3c|thumb=File:YTThumb_cNvmvPa4T3c_CreatorEconomy.webp|title=What's the VRChat Creator Economy?}}|}}
<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
To be able to enroll in the Creator Economy Program, a user must have uploaded content and have access to the VRChat Creator Companion, and then [https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/vrc-econ-apply apply to become a seller], as long as they are eligible:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
====Eligibility<!-- Incomplete. The CE has additional eligibility criteria, listed in the application form: https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/vrc-econ-apply -->====
</div>   

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Be a User who is 18 years of age or older.
* Have a VRChat account that has been active for at least 30 days.
* Have a verified email address associated with your Account.
* Be a community member in good standing at all times while using the Platform, with no suspensions or bans from the Platform or the VRC Creator Economy in the last 90 days.
* Use the Platform in strict compliance with CE Rules, the Terms, the Community Guidelines, and the requirements set out in ''Creator Economy Program Rules Section 5''.
* Not engage in any of the following activities: scamming, phishing, false advertising, attempting to exchange Credits for real currency other than through the Platform, or any illegal or unethical activities.
* Meet any other eligibility requirements that we or our CE Partner may establish from time to time in our or their sole discretion, including but not limited to:
** Having all applicable tax forms on file with the relevant CE Partner
** Completing any applicable CE Partner’s Know Your Customer registration, as required by such CE Partner
{{VRC link|https://hello.vrchat.com/legal/economy |See here}} to view the full Creator Economy Program Rules.
</div>

